From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:18:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: crtc: Let the engine stop its planes when the CRTC
 is disabled

sun4i-drm commits with drm_atomic_helper_commit_tail_rpm(), which
commits planes on active CRTCs only. A plane that is disabled while its
CRTC is inactive, for example because its framebuffer is removed after a
DPMS off, is not written to the hardware, and its buffer can be freed.
When the CRTC is enabled again, the helper enables the CRTC and the
encoder before it commits the planes, so the engine fetches from the
freed buffer until the plane commit. Seen on the Radxa Cubie A7S: after
DPMS off and the close of the DRM master, the fbdev restore enables the
DisplayPort output again, and the IOMMU of the display engine reports
faults on the address of the freed buffer until the planes are written.

Add an optional disable callback to the engine operations and call it
from the CRTC atomic_disable hook, before the TCON stops, so the engine
stops fetching while the CRTC is off. Disabling the planes in the CRTC
disable hook is what drivers with ACTIVE_ONLY plane commits do, such as
Rockchip VOP2 and i.MX DCSS, which call
drm_atomic_helper_disable_planes_on_crtc(). That helper calls the plane
atomic_disable hooks without an atomic state, which the sun4i backend
layers dereference, so the engine does it instead. When the CRTC is
enabled again, the atomic helpers add its planes to the commit, and
their atomic_update writes the layers again.

Not covered: engines without the callback behave as before; the sun8i
mixer implements it in the next patch.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: on its DE33, after the display was blanked
and its framebuffer freed, enabling the CRTC again raises no IOMMU
fault; not tested on DE2 or DE3.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_crtc.c   |  2 ++
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sunxi_engine.h | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_crtc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_crtc.c
index 8219ccb710cd..a7488b6077af 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_crtc.c
@@ -126,6 +126,8 @@ static void sun4i_crtc_atomic_disable(struct drm_crtc *crtc,
 
 	drm_crtc_vblank_off(crtc);
 
+	sunxi_engine_disable(scrtc->engine, crtc);
+
 	sun4i_tcon_set_status(scrtc->tcon, encoder, false);
 
 	if (crtc->state->event && !crtc->state->active) {
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sunxi_engine.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sunxi_engine.h
index 1711c274a41b..37dd4a95d878 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sunxi_engine.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sunxi_engine.h
@@ -123,6 +123,20 @@ struct sunxi_engine_ops {
 	 */
 	void (*mode_set)(struct sunxi_engine *engine,
 			 const struct drm_display_mode *mode);
+
+	/**
+	 * @disable:
+	 *
+	 * This callback is run when the CRTC is disabled, before its
+	 * timing controller stops. The engine has to stop fetching from
+	 * the framebuffers of its planes: the atomic helpers do not
+	 * commit plane changes while the CRTC is inactive, so a buffer
+	 * can be freed before the CRTC is enabled again, and the CRTC is
+	 * enabled before its planes are committed.
+	 *
+	 * This function is optional.
+	 */
+	void (*disable)(struct sunxi_engine *engine, struct drm_crtc *crtc);
 };
 
 /**
@@ -218,4 +232,16 @@ sunxi_engine_mode_set(struct sunxi_engine *engine,
 	if (engine->ops && engine->ops->mode_set)
 		engine->ops->mode_set(engine, mode);
 }
+
+/**
+ * sunxi_engine_disable - Stop the engine's planes when the CRTC is disabled
+ * @engine:	pointer to the engine
+ * @crtc:	pointer to the crtc the engine is associated with
+ */
+static inline void
+sunxi_engine_disable(struct sunxi_engine *engine, struct drm_crtc *crtc)
+{
+	if (engine->ops && engine->ops->disable)
+		engine->ops->disable(engine, crtc);
+}
 #endif /* _SUNXI_ENGINE_H_ */
